{"step_index":13,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T07:49:17Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm currently focused on how best to approach the available tools. I'm prioritizing the most specific tools for each task. It's becoming clear that efficiency is key, so choosing the right tool upfront is essential for streamlined operations. My goal is to minimize wasted steps.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Execution**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on more effective tool execution. Remembering the critical instructions, I’ve adjusted my approach to address PowerShell quoting issues with inline scripts. I’m now leaning towards using `write_to_file` to create Python scripts externally and then execute them, instead of trying to shoehorn everything into a single inline call. This strategy feels much cleaner and less prone to errors.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import re\n\ndef process_file():\n    with open(r'C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\college\\College sem 5\\bie artifacts\\BIE_complete_answer_bank.md', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        content = f.read()\n\n    # Split by '## Q' to isolate questions\n    parts = re.split(r'(?=## Q\\d+)', content)\n    \n    output_lines = []\n    for part in parts:\n        if not part.strip():\n            continue\n            \n        # Bold headings\n        part = re.sub(r'(?m)^#+\\s+(.+)', r'**\\1**', part)\n        \n        # We want to replace '---' with a placeholder so it's not removed\n        part = part.replace('---', ' D_A_S_H_E_S ')\n        \n        # Replace '**' with a placeholder\n        part = part.replace('**', ' B_O_L_D ')\n        \n        # Keep letters, numbers, spaces, bullets, slashes. Replace everything else with space.\n        allowed_chars = set('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789 \\t\\n\\r•/')\n        \n        # Since we added placeholders with underscores, allow underscore temporarily\n        allowed_chars.add('_')\n        \n        res = []\n        for char in part:\n            if char in allowed_chars:\n                res.append(char)\n            else:\n                res.append(' ')\n                \n        text = ''.join(res)\n        \n        # Restore placeholders\n        text = text.replace('B_O_L_D', '**')\n        text = text.replace('D_A_S_H_E_S', '---')\n        \n        # Remove underscores just in case there were real ones (they should be spaces per rules)\n        # Wait, if we replace _ with space, we might break the placeholders. \n        # But we already restored placeholders. Now we can replace any remaining underscores with spaces.\n        text = text.replace('_', ' ')\n        \n        # Clean multiple spaces and newlines\n        text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip()\n        \n        output_lines.append(text)\n\n    final_output = '\\n'.join(output_lines)\n    \n    with open(r'C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\formatted_bank.md', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(final_output)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    process_file()\n","Description":"Python script to format the BIE answer bank","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\format_script.py","toolAction":"Writing formatting script","toolSummary":"Write formatting script"}}]}
